vCU Cells Status Should Be As Expected
    [Arguments]  ${cells_id_list}   ${gnb_index}=0   ${webem_password}=${EMPTY}
    ...   ${administrative_state}=${None}  ${operational_state}=${None}
    ...   ${log_level}=DEBUG
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to check specified vcu cell status should be as expected.
    ...
    ...    *AUTHOR* chris.l.cao@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...    | =Input Parameters= | =Man= | =Description= |
    ...    | cells_id_list | Yes | vdu cell id  list, [1, 2, 3]  |
    ...    | gnb_index     | No  | gnb index in testline configurtion file. Default is 0. |
    ...    | webem_password | No | default value is EMPTY will get from file init |
    ...    | administrative_state | No | Expected administrative state for cell, e.g Unlocked, default is ${None} |
    ...    | operational_state    | No | Expected operational_state for cell, e.g enabled, default is ${None} |
    ...
    ...    *RETURN VALUE*
    ...    None
    ...
    ...    Example
    ...    | ${cell_id_list} | Create List | 1 | 2 | 3 |
    ...    | vCU Cells Status Should Be As Expected | cell_id_list=${cell_id_list} | administrative_state=Unlocked |
    ${unexpected}  set variable  ${False}
    ${conn_alias}    generic_utils.get_unique_id_string
    vcu_gen.login_rest   gnb_index=${gnb_index}   alias=${conn_alias}   webem_password=${webem_password}
    ${cells_status_info}   vcu_ope_business.get_all_vcu_cells_statuses    conn_alias=${conn_alias}
    FOR    ${cell_id}    IN    @{cells_id_list}
        ${r}  Run Keyword And Continue On Failure  generic_utils.member_should_not_contain
            ...  condition_key=id  condition_value=${cell_id}  info_list=${cells_status_info}  log_level=${log_level}
            ...  administrative_state=${administrative_state}  operational_state=${operational_state}
    ${unexpected}    Evaluate   ${unexpected} or ${r}
    END
    Should Not Be True  ${unexpected}  msg=Has cell with unexpected status, please check the error message!!
    [Teardown]    vcu_gen.logout_rest    conn_alias=${conn_alias}


